            {
              "title": "Research Software Developer",
              "caption": "Aug 2020 - Oct 2022 · 2 yrs 2 mos",
              "metadata": "London, England, United Kingdom",
              "description": [
                {
                  "type": "textComponent",
                  "text": "Research Software Developer within the UCL Centre For Advanced Research Computing. An exciting consultancy-style role that allowed me to work with researchers from across the University. I worked extensively in a MLOps-oriented role within a machine learning-driven project to forecast bed demand in hospitals. I also built an end-to-end pipeline to implement and fine-tune several classes of machine learning models for text classification in a social science scenario.\n\nSome of the technologies I regularly used and interacted in this role were:\n- Python\n- PyTorch\n- MLFlow\n- Apache Airflow\n- Docker\n- Kubernetes\n- Tensorflow"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "title": "Postdoctoral Research Associate",
              "caption": "Feb 2021 - Feb 2022 · 1 yr",
              "metadata": "London, England, United Kingdom",
              "description": [
                {
                  "type": "textComponent",
                  "text": "One year part-time secondment as an NLP researcher in the UCL Social Research Institute within the Institute of Education. During this project I led the technical design and implementation of a Python-based software package to implement, train and test several machine learning models, comparing the performance of a 'classical' ML solution to state-of-the-art Transformer-based models and other neural network architectures within classification problems using longitudinal survey data. This PyTorch-driven project used several ML Ops methodologies to track experiment performance and dataset versioning, with peer-reviewed results published."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "companyId": "12766",
