          "subtitle": "The British Library . undefined",
          "caption": "May 2019 - Aug 2020 · 1 yr 3 mos",
          "metadata": "London, United Kingdom",
          "breakdown": false,
          "subComponents": [
            {
              "description": {
                "type": "textComponent",
                "text": "I worked within the Endangered Archive Programme (EAP) to train and deploy convolutional neural networks for supervised learning on classification tasks. I used several cloud platforms including AWS and Google Cloud Platform (GCP) with the fastai and PyTorch Python libraries to determine the orientation of digitised items within the EAP collection. \n\nOther key aspects of my position included:\n\n- Explaining key machine learning concepts to colleagues\n- Delivering tutorials in popular Python data science and data visualisation libraries\n- Supervising students undergoing a PGCert qualification in Python and SQL\n- Working both autonomously and closely with other developers to determine solutions to problems encountered by research colleagues\n- Developing and maintaining C# software frameworks to ingest digitised copies of library collection items"
              }
            }
          ]
